+## Conversation list
+
+To let an authenticated client show a conversation picker, enable `transport.history` in addition to `transport.resume` (the complete setting is in the [full configuration](#full-configuration)). The client sends `{type: 'list_sessions', limit?, before?}` and receives a `session_list` containing metadata-only summaries for that authenticated user. The server ignores any user id in the frame and serialises each summary's `createdAt` and `updatedAt` as ISO strings.
+
+The returned `sessionId` can be reopened by reconnecting to `/ws?sessionId=<id>`. Keep resume enabled if clients need that affordance: history listing without resume can show ids that the transport will not rejoin. Paging passes the last summary back as `before`; use the store's retention and erasure controls to bound the personal metadata exposed by the list (see [session stores](session-stores.md#listing-a-users-conversations) and [GDPR guidance](../specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md#security-considerations)).
